From 8842826e5d6f2bd6ac3c7cf82862baa011f09970 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:48:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] google-grouping: job families for Google from titles,
 brand kept as its own field

- server/families.js: deterministic title classifier into 27 job families modelled on
  Google's careers categories (Software Engineering, Technical Program Management, Data
  Center Operations, Technical Solutions, Sales, ...); null when a title names no role.
  Pure ES with no imports, so it is in server/lib-modules.js's browser-safe list
  (sources/google.js imports it).
- server/sources/google.js: department = the title's family (departmentBasis 'title'),
  brand = Google's brand (Google, YouTube, DeepMind, Waymo, ...), team stays the brand.
  upgradeGoogleJobs gives stored snapshots the same at read time (idempotent).
- test/fixtures/google-families-sample.json: 320 hand-labelled titles (tuning 120,
  held-out 100, fresh 100 from the 2026-10-16 crawl).
- test/google-grouping.test.js: accuracy, coverage, brand, read-time upgrade.
- test/fix-beta-sources.test.js: the D-24 test follows the new mapping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
